---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Forum"
  description="Community threads for local Radeon AI. Off on this static build until FORUM_ENABLED."
>
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <p class="kicker">Community</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-3 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Forum</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Threads, solved marks, and rig badges ship behind <code class="font-mono text-ink">FORUM_ENABLED</code>, which also needs accounts. This public build stays static so a crawler never hits a database.
    </p>
    <div class="card mt-8 p-6">
      <p class="kicker">Planned categories</p>
      <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-2 text-sm text-muted sm:grid-cols-2">
        <li>Getting Started</li>
        <li>Install &amp; Drivers</li>
        <li>llama.cpp</li>
        <li>Strata</li>
        <li>vLLM</li>
        <li>Ollama / LM Studio</li>
        <li>Image &amp; Video Gen</li>
        <li>Hardware &amp; Builds</li>
        <li>Abliterated Models</li>
        <li>Benchmarks</li>
        <li>Show Your Rig</li>
        <li>Site Feedback</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm">
        <a class="btn-secondary" href="/account">Saved rigs first</a>
        <a class="btn-ghost ml-2" href="/troubleshoot/errors">Paste an error</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
